Andrew Fabbro wrote:
> Corpses rot after 50 turns, which means you have to kill them near the
> altar...

If monsters become really huge and too heavy to lift you even have to
lure them onto the altar to kill them.

> and often if you find a coaligned altar on level 1 or 3 or so
> forth, there aren't that many monsters around.

Descend deeper and come back later when more types of monsters will be
generated. (Depending on max dungeon level and your experience level.)

> Is a wand/scroll/book of create monster a necessary requirement for a
> "sac fest"?

It helps, of course, but it's not necessary. Later on you'll also find
hordes of monsters generated, rothes, orcs, killer bees.

If your altar is close enough to the stairs (and the monster corpses not
too heavy to lift) you can search monster on the adjacent level and drag
them to the altar.

If you're tough enough to handle it you can try to read cursed scrolls
of create monster, or break a wand of create monster preferable when it
has one charge left, to get a bunch of sacrifice fodder.

Engraving reliably, fast, and persistent the E-word also helps to handle
the hordes of monsters.

